  "requestTimestamp": "2026-07-19T01:33:22.171Z",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe ₱5,000,000 standard deduction for estate tax is a tax-free threshold, not a deduction. It allows the estate to exclude this amount from the gross estate before calculating the estate tax due.\n\n### Interpretation\nThe ₱5,000,000 standard deduction serves as a threshold that reduces the taxable estate amount. This means that estates valued at or below this threshold are not subject to estate tax, effectively exempting them from taxation up to that limit. It is not treated as a deduction from the gross estate but rather as an exclusion that determines the taxable base.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor estate planning and tax compliance, this standard deduction simplifies the process for estates valued at ₱5,000,000 or less, as they will not incur any estate tax liability. Executors and beneficiaries should be aware of this threshold when assessing the estate's value and planning for tax obligations.",
